.Dd @MDOCDATE@
.Dt CLOWN-STDIO-BRIDGE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm clown-stdio-bridge
.Nd bridge a stdio MCP server to streamable-HTTP for clown-plugin-host
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -listen-unix Ar path Fl -peer-unit Ar unit
.Fl -command Ar cmd
.Cm --
.Op Ar args
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
wraps a JSON-RPC-over-stdio MCP server and exposes it on an ephemeral
loopback HTTP port speaking the streamable-HTTP MCP transport.
The wrapped server is spawned as a child process; its stdin and stdout
are driven by
.Nm Ap s
translator goroutines.
.Pp
.Nm
is launched by
.Xr clown-plugin-host 1
as the synthesized command for any
.Li stdioServers
entry in
.Xr clown-json 5 .
Plugin authors do not invoke
.Nm
directly; they declare a stdio MCP server in
.Pa clown.json
and clown desugars it into a
.Li httpServers
entry pointing at this binary.
The desugaring lets stdio-declared servers and native HTTP servers share
a single discovery and lifecycle path under
.Xr clown-plugin-host 1 .
.Pp
On launch
.Nm
prints the same handshake line as a native clown-plugin server (see
.Xr clown-plugin-protocol 7 ) ,
binds
.Li 127.0.0.1:0 ,
and serves
.Li GET /healthz
and
.Li {GET,POST,DELETE} /mcp ,
plus the clown control routes
.Li GET /clown/system-prompt
and
.Li {GET,POST} /clown/exclude-tools .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -listen-unix Ar path Fl -peer-unit Ar unit
Serve on the unix socket
.Ar path
(absolute; created 0600 in a 0700 directory) instead of loopback TCP, and
announce the unix handshake form.
Each connection is admitted only from a process in the systemd unit
.Ar unit Ns 's
cgroup (SO_PEERCRED) or from the bridge's parent clown.
The control routes answer 403 to the unit.
A socket that still answers is not taken over.
The bridge exits once its parent is gone.
clown uses this for a confined session's spinclass serve (FDR 0020 F12);
the two flags go together.
.It Fl -command Ar cmd
The wrapped stdio MCP server binary.
Resolved against the caller's
.Ev PATH
via
.Xr execvp 3 ;
absolute paths bypass lookup.
Required.
.It Cm --
Separator between
.Nm
flags and the wrapped command's argv.
Everything after
.Cm --
is taken verbatim as the wrapped command's arguments, including any
literal
.Cm --
tokens.
.El
.Sh PROTOCOL TRANSLATION
.Nm
implements a subset of the streamable-HTTP MCP transport sufficient to
bridge a stdio MCP server with no client-side awareness:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Li POST /mcp Pq JSON-RPC request
The body is forwarded verbatim, followed by a newline, to the wrapped
child's stdin.
.Nm
waits for a JSON-RPC response with the matching
.Li id
on the child's stdout.
By default the response is delivered as a
.Li text/event-stream
.Pq SSE
whose terminal
.Li data:
event carries the JSON-RPC response, with periodic keep-alive heartbeats
emitted while the call is in flight
.Pq see Sx ENVIRONMENT .
When streaming is disabled
.Pq Ev CLOWN_BRIDGE_HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL Ns = Ns Li 0
the response is instead a synchronous
.Li application/json
body.
.It Li POST /mcp Pq JSON-RPC notification or response
The body is forwarded fire-and-forget; the HTTP layer responds with
.Li 202 Accepted
immediately.
.It Li GET /mcp
Opens a Server-Sent Events stream.
Server-initiated JSON-RPC messages from the wrapped child
.Pq i.e., lines on its stdout that have a Li method No field but no matching pending Li id
are broadcast to every active SSE subscriber as
.Li data:\& Ns Ar payload
events.
.It Li DELETE /mcp
Returns
.Li 405 Method Not Allowed .
Session termination is not supported in v1; the bridge does not assign
session IDs.
.El
.Pp
The
.Li Origin
header is restricted to loopback origins
.Pq Li 127.0.0.1 , Li ::1 , Li localhost
or absent, per the streamable-HTTP spec's DNS-rebinding mitigation.
Other origins receive
.Li 403 Forbidden .
.Sh RESOURCE LIMITS
.Nm
caps the number of pending JSON-RPC messages in each direction at a
fixed depth.
On overflow:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy Inbound Pq HTTP No -> child stdin
The offending HTTP request receives a JSON-RPC error response with code
.Li \-32000
and message
.Dq clown-stdio-bridge: inbound queue saturated .
The wrapped child stays alive.
.It Sy Outbound Pq child stdout No -> SSE subscriber
The oldest pending broadcast in the offending subscriber's channel is
dropped to make room.
A counter
.Pq exposed via Sy DroppedOutbound
records the cumulative drop count.
.El
.Pp
The depth is a tuning parameter and may change between minor versions.
.Sh CRASH BEHAVIOR
If the wrapped child exits unexpectedly,
.Nm
logs the exit status and itself exits non-zero.
.Xr clown-plugin-host 1 Ap s
existing failure path
.Pq Li StartReport.Failed , Fl -skip-failed
handles restart-or-abort.
.Nm
is a transport adapter, not a supervisor.
.Pp
The bridge also exits when it can no longer talk to a child that is still
running: the child's stdout reaches end of file, or a write to its stdin
fails.
.Sh DISCONNECT RECORDS
When the host gave the bridge a record identity
.Pq see Ev CLOWN_BRIDGE_RECORD_DIR ,
the bridge writes one JSON record for each way it sees its child's session
end: the child exiting, its stdout reaching end of file, a failed write to its
stdin, a signal, the host going away, or the HTTP server failing.
The record holds the time, the kind, who closed it, the child's exit status,
the requests in flight and abandoned, the queue depth, and the last 40 lines
of the child's stderr, scrubbed as described below.
It never holds request or response content.
.Pp
The scrub is best effort, not a guarantee.
It turns control characters into spaces, drops other non-printing characters,
and cuts a line to 512 bytes; it replaces the value of
.Li key=value ,
.Li key: value
and the same pairs written as quoted JSON, whose key contains
.Li token ,
.Li key ,
.Li secret
or
.Li password ;
the value of a command-line flag whose name contains one of them;
.Li Bearer
tokens;
.Li Authorization: token
and
.Li Authorization: Basic
values; the user and password of a URL
.Pq Li scheme://user:pass@host ;
tokens with the prefixes
.Li sk- ,
.Li ghp_ ,
.Li gho_ ,
.Li ghu_ ,
.Li ghs_ ,
.Li ghr_ ,
.Li xox
and
.Li AKIA ;
hex runs of 32 or more characters; and base64-looking runs of 40 or more
characters that hold both letters and digits.
It does not catch a secret whose key or flag has none of those four words
.Pq for example Li pw=x No or Li passphrase ,
a secret written in prose, a short bare token, a multi-line key block line by
line, or anything the child prints in a form not listed here.
Treat the tail as sensitive.
Records are files named
.Pa <n>.json
under
.Pa <record dir>/<hex sha256 of the session key>/<plugin>/<server>/ ,
written atomically; at most 20 are kept per server, and a session's whole
directory is removed 30 days after its newest record.
.Pp
Every request in flight when the child goes away fails with a JSON-RPC error
(code
.Li -32001 )
whose message states the kind and exit status, and names the record's
resource URI and the MCP server
.Li clown-builtin-diagnostics/disconnects
that serves it.
The host's death of a bridge is recorded by the host as kind
.Li bridge_exit .
The records are read with
.Xr clown 1
.Cm disconnects .
.Pp
.Li POST /clown/shutdown
(loopback, origin-checked, no body) tells the bridge that the SIGTERM about to
follow is the host stopping it on purpose; the bridge then writes no record
for that signal.
.Sh SHUTDOWN
On
.Dv SIGTERM
or
.Dv SIGINT ,
.Nm
sends
.Dv SIGTERM
to the wrapped child's process group, waits up to 5 seconds for clean
exit, then escalates to
.Dv SIGKILL .
The HTTP server is gracefully shut down on the same path.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev CLOWN_BRIDGE_RECORD_DIR
The directory disconnect records are written under.
Set by the plugin host together with
.Ev CLOWN_SESSION_ID ,
.Ev CLOWN_BRIDGE_PLUGIN_NAME
and
.Ev CLOWN_BRIDGE_SERVER_NAME ;
without all four the bridge writes no records.
.It Ev CLOWN_SESSION_ID
The session's key, as the record's session; the records directory is named by
its hash.
Set by the plugin host.
.It Ev CLOWN_BRIDGE_PLUGIN_NAME
The plugin's name, as the record's plugin.
.It Ev CLOWN_BRIDGE_HOST_LOG
Path of the host's log, copied into the record so a reader knows where the
host's side is.
.It Ev CLOWN_BRIDGE_HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL
Cadence of the keep-alive heartbeats emitted on streaming
.Li POST /mcp
responses while the bridge waits for the wrapped child's reply.
Parsed by
.Xr time.ParseDuration 3 .
Default:
.Li 30s .
The values
.Li 0 ,
.Li off ,
and the empty string disable streaming entirely: the response falls back
to a synchronous
.Li application/json
body, and child notifications are not forwarded on that POST.
A negative or unparseable value is ignored in favor of the default.
.It Ev CLOWN_BRIDGE_HEARTBEAT
Named heartbeat mode that overrides the interval-derived policy.
The recognized value
.Li forward-only
.Pq alias Li child
keeps streaming and child-notification forwarding on but suppresses the
bridge's own timer, so keep-alive becomes
.Em activity-driven \(em
carried solely by the wrapped child's own
.Li notifications/progress .
This lets a genuinely silent child time out instead of being held open
indefinitely by a blind timer.
.Pp
The value
.Li forward-only+fallback
.Pq alias Li child+fallback
is the same, but additionally arms an
.Em activity-gated
fallback timer: the bridge emits a heartbeat only after the child has been
silent for the
.Ev CLOWN_BRIDGE_HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL
threshold
.Pq default when that is unset or Li 0 ,
re-arming on every message the child emits.
This gives a bridge-side keep-alive ceiling for a slow-but-progressing call
while still letting a genuinely hung child stop re-arming and time out.
.Pp
Unset or any unrecognized value falls back to the
.Ev CLOWN_BRIDGE_HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL
cadence.
.It Ev STATSD_HOST , Ev STATSD_PORT
Destination for the bridge's statsd metrics (stats-me), fire-and-forget
UDP.
Defaults:
.Li 127.0.0.1
and
.Li 8125 .
Every bridged JSON-RPC request emits, under
.Li clown.bridge.<server>.<label>. \(em
where
.Li <server>
comes from
.Ev CLOWN_BRIDGE_SERVER_NAME
and
.Li <label>
is the tool name for
.Li tools/call
.Pq else the JSON-RPC method ,
both sanitized to
.Li [A-Za-z0-9_-] \(em
a
.Li .duration
timer
.Pq Li |ms , No on completed responses
plus exactly one outcome counter
.Pq Li |c :
.Li .success ,
.Li .failure
.Pq JSON-RPC error response, bridge error, or queue-full ,
or
.Li .abandoned
.Pq client disconnected before a response .
Emission never blocks or fails the request path; when nothing listens the
datagrams are simply dropped.
.It Ev CLOWN_DISABLE_STATSD
When set to
.Li 1 ,
disables statsd emission entirely.
.It Ev CLOWN_BRIDGE_SERVER_NAME
Logical name of the bridged server, used as the statsd metric prefix
segment and as the record's server.
Set automatically by
.Nm clown Ns 's
.Fa stdioServers
desugaring
.Pq see Xr clown-json 5 ;
defaults to
.Li unknown
when unset.
.El
.Pp
For how these heartbeats interact with Claude Code's per-tool
.Fa timeout ,
see the
.Dq Request Timeout Regimes
section of
.Xr clown-json 5 .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits
.Li 0
on a clean
.Dv SIGTERM Ns / Ns Dv SIGINT
shutdown after spawning the wrapped child successfully.
Exit status
.Li 1
indicates an error reachable before or during the wrapped child's
lifetime: missing or invalid flags, command lookup failure, network
listen failure, HTTP serve error, or unexpected child exit.
